        "message": "That makes financial independence the most urgent priority, because having your own rent covered gives you full autonomy. Given that constraint, here are two realistic ways to play this: 1. **The Dual-Track Approach**\nTake a stable, paying job now—even if it isn't your dream role—to cover your own rent and build an emergency fund. Treat your evenings and weekends as your design studio to build a portfolio, take courses, or land small client projects. Once you can pay your own rent, their leverage drops, and you can switch to design full-time on your own terms. 2. **The Time-Boxed Proposal**\nIf you want to pursue design immediately without taking a detour, ask them for a specific, agreed-upon window (such as 3 to 6 months) while they cover rent. Show them a concrete plan: the exact salaried roles you’re targeting (like junior UI or production design), your daily study/portfolio schedule, and a clear backup plan: if you don’t land a paying role by the deadline, you will pivot to the stable job they prefer. The first option gives you control faster; the second asks for a temporary compromise with built-in accountability.",
